Description: A language/voice set with only the voice GNUstep uses
 flite's configure --with-langvox=<name> selects config/<name>.lv, which lists
 the lexicons, languages and voices to build. The shipped sets build six or
 more voices (about 60 MiB). This one builds cmu_us_kal16, the voice
 gnustep-gui's speech server registers (Tools/speech/FliteSpeechEngine.m calls
 register_cmu_us_kal16(), and gnustep-gui's configure only builds the speech
 tools when -lflite_cmu_us_kal16 links), with the US English language and the
 CMU lexicon it is built on. EXTRABINS is empty: flite_time needs the
 cmu_time_awb voice.
Origin: NextBSD
Forwarded: not-needed (NextBSD's selection)
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/config/nextbsd.lv
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+#
+#  NextBSD: the one voice GNUstep's speech server uses (gnustep-gui
+#  Tools/speech/FliteSpeechEngine.m registers cmu_us_kal16), with the US
+#  English language and the CMU lexicon it needs. No extra programs
+#  (flite_time needs the cmu_time_awb voice).
+LEXES = cmulex
+LANGS = usenglish
+VOXES = cmu_us_kal16
+EXTRABINS =
